{{/*
family: line-cli
what: syslog
transports: udp, tcp, tls
reference: common line-oriented logging commands (logging host, logging trap, logging facility, logging source-interface); RFC 5424 severities
verification: reference
*/}}
{{define "does"}}Sends the device's log messages, {{.Severity.Word}} and more severe, to Woodshed over {{if eq .Transport "udp"}}UDP{{else if eq .Transport "tcp"}}TCP{{else}}TLS{{end}}.{{end}}

{{define "parts"}}
@@part cli - Enter in global configuration mode, fill in the placeholders, then save the configuration
logging host {{.Address}}{{if eq .Transport "tcp"}} <TCP-OPTION>{{else if eq .Transport "tls"}} <TLS-OPTION>{{else if ne .Port 514}} <UDP-PORT-OPTION>{{end}}
logging trap {{.Severity.Line}}
{{- if .Facility}}
logging facility {{.Facility}}{{end}}
{{- if .SourceInterface}}
logging source-interface {{.SourceInterface}}{{end}}
{{end}}

{{define "notes"}}
{{if eq .Transport "tcp"}}<TCP-OPTION> is the device's way of saying TCP to port {{.Port}} on the host line. It differs between devices (a transport keyword with a port, a protocol/port pair after the address, or a separate command), so take it from the device's documentation.
{{else if eq .Transport "tls"}}<TLS-OPTION> is the device's way of saying TLS to port {{.Port}} on the host line, and often naming the trusted CA. It differs between devices, so take it from the device's documentation.
{{else if ne .Port 514}}<UDP-PORT-OPTION> is the device's way of naming UDP port {{.Port}} on the host line (Woodshed doesn't use the usual 514); it differs between devices.
{{else}}`logging host {{.Address}}` alone sends over UDP to port 514 on most devices of this style.
{{end}}
{{- if eq .Transport "tls"}}Import Woodshed's CA certificate as a trusted CA first (Settings → TLS → CA certificate: PEM to paste, DER to upload){{if .CASHA256}}, and compare the fingerprint the device shows with {{.CASHA256}}{{end}}. How you import it differs by device.
If the device checks the server's name, give it {{.TLSName}}{{if .TLSNameKnown}}, a name on Woodshed's certificate{{else}} (it must be a DNS name on Woodshed's certificate; Settings → TLS lists them once TLS is on){{end}}; many devices check names only, not IP addresses.
{{end}}
`logging trap` sets the lowest severity sent to log hosts on many devices; others set it on the host line, or accept the number ({{.Severity.Num}}) instead of the keyword.
{{- if .SourceInterface}}
The source interface's address is what Woodshed shows as the device, so pick one with a stable address.
{{- end}}
Turn on timestamps in the messages if the device offers it (with milliseconds and the time zone, where it can); Woodshed also keeps the time each message arrived.
{{end}}

{{define "check"}}The device appears on Woodshed's Dashboard with its first message; if it doesn't, check the device's log host status and Woodshed's Listeners on the Setup page.{{end}}
